{title: 655 - Happy the Home}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Home}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Happy the [Am/C]home [Bm]when [Am]God [D]is [G]there,
[D7/A]And love [G]fills [D/F#]every breast;
[Am]When one their wish, and [D]one their prayer,
[Bm]And one [C]their heavenly [G]rest.

Verse 2:
[G]Happy the [Am/C]home [Bm]where [Am]Jesus' [G]name
[D7/A]is sweet [G]to [D/F#]every ear;
[Am]where children early [D]speak his fame,
[Bm]and [C]parents [G/D]hold [D7]him [G]dear.

Verse 3:
[G]Happy the [Am/C]home [Bm]where [Am]prayer [D]is [G]heard,
[D7/A]and [G]praise [D/F#]is [G]wont [Em]to [D]rise;
[Am]where parents love the [D]sacred Word
[Bm]and [C]all its [G/D]wisdom prize.

Verse 4:
[G]Lord, let us in [Am/C]our [Bm]homes [D]agree
[D7/A]this [G]blessed [D/F#]peace [G]to [Em]gain;
[Am]unite our hearts in [D]love to thee,
[Bm]and [C]love to [G/D]all [D7]will [G]reign.
